{%- doc -%}
  Malaysia-only pages (2026-10). Shoppers outside Malaysia (Singapore) don't
  get them: the page itself sends them to the home page, and links to it are
  left out. The list is my_only_paths below; today just the clearance sale.
  Region-locked products use custom.only_market instead (layout/theme.liquid).

  part 'head'  : in <head> of layout/theme.liquid. On a listed page, the
                 redirect (not in the theme editor, so the page can still be
                 edited while previewing Singapore). On every page, CSS that
                 hides links to the listed pages: menu items (header, mobile
                 drawer, footer), search suggestions and any other link.
  part 'check' : prints "hidden" when url points to a listed page. Homepage
                 banners (sections/apgo-home-carousel.liquid) use it to drop
                 the whole slide, so the slide count and dots stay right.

  @param {string} part - 'head' or 'check'.
  @param {string} [url] - The link to check, for part 'check'.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign my_only_paths = '/pages/clearance-sale' | split: ','
  assign outside_my = false
  if localization.country.iso_code != 'MY'
    assign outside_my = true
  endif
  # Shopify serves /pages/Clearance-Sale too, so compare in lower case.
  assign apgo_mo_path = request.path | downcase
  assign apgo_mo_url = url | downcase
-%}
{%- if outside_my -%}
  {%- if part == 'check' -%}
    {%- for path in my_only_paths -%}
      {%- if apgo_mo_url contains path -%}hidden{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- elsif part == 'head' -%}
    {%- unless request.design_mode -%}
      {%- for path in my_only_paths -%}
        {%- if apgo_mo_path contains path -%}
          <script>window.location.replace({{ routes.root_url | json }});</script>
          {%- break -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endunless -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      One rule per selector: a browser without :has() drops a whole rule
      when any selector in it is unknown, which would take the plain link
      rule down with it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <style>
      {%- for path in my_only_paths %}
      a[href*="{{ path }}" i] { display: none !important; }
      li:has(> a[href*="{{ path }}" i]) { display: none !important; }
      .predictive-search-results__card:has(a[href*="{{ path }}" i]) { display: none !important; }
      {%- endfor %}
    </style>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
